# Generated by from_capture.py from a real capture, exactly like the host harness's
# scenarios/. Not in git: the long-arm replay alone is ~23 MB, it is every frame of a
# capture in the project folder (reverse-it) that is not published, and committing a
# generated stimulus is how the two drift apart without anything noticing.
#
# What keeps it honest instead is stimulus.fnv, which IS committed: every replay-driven
# case records a checksum of the stimulus it ran on (spec 12.4), so a regenerated
# scenario that differs fails the case rather than quietly measuring something else.
#
# make builds it, through build_longarm.py; README.md has the details.
scenarios/

shim_test
